    "SignInCall": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Sign a person in at the provider, in two steps (ADR-0111).\n\n``start``: answer the address to send the person to -- the provider's authorization page with\n``redirect_uri``, ``state`` and the PKCE ``code_challenge`` (S256) as given. Korsi made the\nstate and keeps the verifier; the plugin keeps nothing.\n\n``finish``: the provider sent the person back with ``code``. Turn it into the secrets to keep\n(a refresh token, say) with ``code_verifier`` and the same ``redirect_uri``, and say whose\naccount it is. Korsi seals the secrets and hands them back on every later call, as it does a\npassword. ``values`` and ``secrets`` on the envelope are empty: there is no connection yet.",
      "properties": {
        "call": {
          "const": "connection.sign_in",
          "default": "connection.sign_in",
          "title": "Call",
          "type": "string"
